1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:09,550
1919, Boston. A giant 8-metre wave swept through the city streets... but this wave wasn't water!

2
00:00:12,117 --> 00:00:18,177
January 15, 1919. The North End neighborhood of Boston, in the United States.

3
00:00:18,342 --> 00:00:24,993
For days, it has been freezing cold. But this morning, the air has suddenly warmed up.

4
00:00:25,143 --> 00:00:28,553
People have opened their coats and are enjoying the sun in the streets.

5
00:00:29,992 --> 00:00:33,682
Children are coming home from school, workers are heading out to lunch.

6
00:00:34,783 --> 00:00:39,543
No one knows what is happening inside the giant tank by the harbor.

7
00:00:40,492 --> 00:00:46,682
The tank was 15 metres tall. And it was almost 27 metres wide.

8
00:00:47,242 --> 00:00:52,912
Inside, there were about 8.5 million litres of molasses.

9
00:00:53,825 --> 00:00:59,735
This molasses was used to make industrial alcohol. And that alcohol was used to make ammunition.

10
00:01:01,450 --> 00:01:06,940
The tank had been built in a hurry in 1915. And it had never been tested by filling it with water.

11
00:01:09,408 --> 00:01:14,648
From the very first day, molasses began leaking from parts of the tank.

12
00:01:14,825 --> 00:01:20,685
The company found a solution: it painted the tank brown. That way, the leaks wouldn't show.

13
00:01:21,367 --> 00:01:26,757
Meanwhile, local families collected the leaking molasses in buckets and took it home.

14
00:01:27,700 --> 00:01:33,430
That day, around 12:30 in the afternoon, a strange sound was heard in the neighborhood.

15
00:01:34,533 --> 00:01:38,263
According to witnesses, it sounded like machine-gun fire.

16
00:01:39,283 --> 00:01:42,843
It was the tank's rivets, popping out one by one.

17
00:01:43,867 --> 00:01:47,757
Then the ground shook. Some thought it was the sound of a train.

18
00:01:49,117 --> 00:01:52,847
And the giant tank suddenly burst open.

19
00:01:53,950 --> 00:01:57,590
Millions of litres of molasses poured into the streets.

20
00:01:58,492 --> 00:02:01,712
In some places, the wave was 8 metres high.

21
00:02:05,075 --> 00:02:08,945
And it moved at more than 50 kilometres per hour.

22
00:02:09,658 --> 00:02:14,548
The molasses wave shifted buildings and swept away vehicles and horses.

23
00:02:15,825 --> 00:02:19,315
Even the steel pillars of the nearby railway were bent.

24
00:02:20,408 --> 00:02:25,358
A train driver saw the tracks collapse at the last moment and stopped the train.

25
00:02:26,283 --> 00:02:30,513
Even the neighborhood fire station slid off its foundation.

26
00:02:31,200 --> 00:02:35,550
Molasses wasn't like water. It was thick and sticky.

27
00:02:36,075 --> 00:02:39,225
And in the cold, it became even harder.

28
00:02:40,658 --> 00:02:44,488
People and horses who fell into it just couldn't get free.

29
00:02:45,742 --> 00:02:49,712
Rescuers tried to walk through molasses up to their waists.

30
00:02:50,992 --> 00:02:54,452
Sailors, soldiers and police helped for hours.

31
00:02:56,783 --> 00:03:03,213
Sadly, 21 people lost their lives in this disaster. About 150 people were injured.

32
00:03:04,367 --> 00:03:07,187
Cleaning up the molasses took weeks.

33
00:03:08,700 --> 00:03:13,030
Firefighters sprayed seawater from the harbor onto the streets with hoses.

34
00:03:13,950 --> 00:03:17,570
The salt water slowly dissolved the sticky molasses.

35
00:03:18,533 --> 00:03:22,023
The harbor water stayed brown all summer long.

36
00:03:23,117 --> 00:03:27,287
Stuck to people's shoes, the molasses spread across the whole city.

37
00:03:28,617 --> 00:03:33,787
According to sources, even streetcars, phone booths and houses became sticky.

38
00:03:35,283 --> 00:03:38,103
After the disaster, families sued the company.

39
00:03:39,617 --> 00:03:44,197
At first, the company blamed others and claimed the tank had been blown up in an attack.

40
00:03:45,742 --> 00:03:49,652
But in a case that lasted years, the truth came out.

41
00:03:50,325 --> 00:03:54,645
The tank was too thin for the weight it held, and it was poorly built.

42
00:03:55,492 --> 00:03:59,282
The court found the company guilty and ordered it to pay the families.

43
00:04:01,867 --> 00:04:05,647
After this disaster, building rules in America changed.

44
00:04:06,908 --> 00:04:11,858
From then on, the calculations for large structures had to be signed by engineers.

45
00:04:12,825 --> 00:04:17,185
Today, where the tank once stood, there is a playground and sports fields.

46
00:04:17,867 --> 00:04:23,722
And some people in Boston say that on hot summer days, they can still smell molasses.

47
00:04:25,217 --> 00:04:28,847
Do you think this disaster could have been prevented? See you in the comments.
